<title>DENMARK: FORECAST-Danish Economy Ministry report - main data.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Danish Economy Ministry report - main data.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a table of the main points from the Danish Economy Ministry's October forecast (estimates from last survey in August in brackets).</p>
<p> (Percent growth)	   1996	    1997</p>
<p> GDP			    2.0 (1.8)	3.1 (3.0)</p>
<p> Inflation		    2.1 (2.0)	2.3 (2.3)</p>
<p> Private consumption	2.3 (2.3)	2.8 (2.9)</p>
<p> Exports			3.1 (1.5)	3.9 (3.6)</p>
<p> Imports			1.0 (0.0)	3.5 (3.1)</p>
<p> Unemployment		 8.9 (9.0)	8.4 (8.6)</p>
<p> C/A surplus (bln crowns) 10.3 (10.0)    10.8 (11.5)</p>
<p>Govt public sector deficit (bln crowns)</p>
<p>				 -14.9 (-15.3)  -3.5 (-5.8)</p>
<p>10-yr interest rate (pct/yr)</p>
<p>				  7.3 (7.3)	7.5 (7.5)</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
</text>
